cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:13:Branch `kg/rebuild-trainer-model`, based on `kg/isaiah-gap-closure` at `e1458d2`. The [[kaggriculture-encoder-reuses-isaiah-stateless-layers|encoder]] and [[kaggriculture-grammar-heads-sit-behind-isaiahs-actor-projection|heads]] References left three items open: shared registration, trainer compile wiring, and the critic's masked softmax. This note records all three.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:19:  - `python/owl/model/factory.py`: `create_model` matches on the config class and ends in `assert_never`, as Isaiah's factory does. Each architecture belongs to one game. An Orbit model given Kaggriculture specs raises `TypeError`, and so does the reverse. Overloads give Orbit callers `BaseModelAPI` and Kaggriculture callers `KaggricultureTransformer`. A caller holding the full union gets `BaseModelAPI[Any, Any, Any]`.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:21:- **Trunk compile.**
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:22:  - `TrunkCompileAPI` (`python/owl/model/base.py`) is a nominal ABC with `compile_transformer_trunk(*, mode) -> int`. `StatelessTransformerV1` and `KaggricultureTransformer` both implement it.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:23:  - `configure_model_compile` accepts any `nn.Module`. For `trunk` it dispatches with `isinstance` (no `getattr`). The recurrent model keeps Isaiah's specific error, and any other model raises.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:24:  - Kaggriculture compiles only `_forward_transformer_trunk` (blocks plus `final_norm`). `_run_trunk` calls it after the overflow guard and chunking.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:25:  - `mlp` compiles `blocks[i].mlp` in place, and those modules run only inside `_run_trunk`.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:26:- **Critic.** The Task 2.2 brief asked for a masked winner softmax, and Isaiah uses `masked_softmax(logits, still_playing)`. The code used a plain `log_softmax`.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:27:  - `_winner_log_probabilities` now follows Isaiah's `_critic_distillation`. It fills masked logits with the dtype minimum, then applies `log_softmax`.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:29:  - Live rows are unchanged. An all-masked row gets Isaiah's uniform masked result (value 0).
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:30:  - **Recorded deviation:** Isaiah's `_critic_logits` raises on a row with no live player; this model does not. The heads already emit empty programs for inactive rows, and contract v4 keeps `still_playing` true. The difference is listed in `docs/kaggriculture-model.md` (resolved toward Isaiah's output, not escalated).
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:41:- `tests/kaggriculture/test_model_compile.py` (11 tests):
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:42:  - the trunk target compiles exactly the bound `_forward_transformer_trunk` with `dynamic=True`
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:43:  - over sampling, replay and value calls, only block submodules and `final_norm` run inside the compiled region. Stems, critic, actor projection and heads run outside it.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:44:  - the compiled callable is called once per chunk, and the guard raises before it runs
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:45:  - `mlp` compiles exactly the block MLPs, and they run only inside `_run_trunk`
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:46:  - no target compiles the whole model
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:47:  - an AST pin lists every compile call site on the trainer and model paths
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:48:  - Against the base dispatch, 4 of these fail (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/trainer-model/compile-red.log`).
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic.md:51:  - with distinct non-zero critic tokens on every row, the probabilities equal Isaiah's `masked_softmax`, live rows equal the unmasked softmax, and finished rows are uniform with value 0
